To organize and analyze the given data, you can use Java along with libraries like Apache POI for reading Excel tables and processing the data. Here is a sample code snippet:

```java
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.IOException;
import org.apache.poi.ss.usermodel.*;

public class MagneticFieldAnalyzer {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        FileInputStream file = new FileInputStream("earth_magnetic_field_data.xlsx");
        Workbook workbook = WorkbookFactory.create(file);
        Sheet sheet = workbook.getSheetAt(0);

        // Iterate through each row in the sheet
        for (Row row : sheet) {
            Cell locationCell = row.getCell(0);
            Cell latitudeCell = row.getCell(1);
            Cell longitudeCell = row.getCell(2);
            Cell intensityCell = row.getCell(3);

            // Extract the values from the cells
            String location = locationCell.getStringCellValue();
            double latitude = latitudeCell.getNumericCellValue();
            double longitude = longitudeCell.getNumericCellValue();
            double intensity = intensityCell.getNumericCellValue();

            // Process the data as needed
            System.out.printf("%s (%f, %f): %.2f Tesla%n", location, latitude, longitude, intensity);
        }

        workbook.close();
        file.close();
    }
}
```

