% Convert to grayscale
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);

% Apply Gaussian filter
gaussian_filter = fspecial('gaussian', [5 5], 0.5);
filtered_image = imfilter(gray_image, gaussian_filter);

% Define Sobel operator in x direction
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];

% Define Sobel operator in y direction
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];

% Apply Sobel operator in x direction
edge_image_x = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_x, 'same');

% Apply Sobel operator in y direction
edge_image_y = conv2(double(filtered_image), sobel_y, 'same');

% Combine edges in both directions
edge_image = sqrt(edge_image_x.^2 + edge_image_y.^2);

% Display edge image
imshow(edge_image);
```

In this modified code, we first apply a Gaussian filter to the grayscale image using the `imfilter` function. The `fspecial` function is used to create a Gaussian filter kernel with a size of 5x5 pixels and a standard deviation of 0.5. The `conv2` function is then used to convolve the filtered image with the Sobel operators in both the x and y directions. Finally, the edges are combined and displayed using the `imshow` function.

This modified code should help reduce the noise in the image and improve the accuracy of the edge detection.

