To register your GoDaddy domain with your personal Linux machine, you can follow these steps:

1. Create an account on the GoDaddy website and purchase a domain name.
2. Log in to your GoDaddy account and navigate to the "Domain" tab.
3. Click on the "Manage DNS" button next to the domain you want to register.
4. In the "Nameservers" section, click on the "Use Custom Nameservers" option.
5. Enter the IP addresses of your personal Linux machine's nameservers in the "Custom Nameservers" field. You can find the IP addresses by running the following command on your Linux machine:
```bash
ip addr show
```
6. Click on the "Save" button to update your domain's nameservers.
7. On your Linux machine, install the BIND software by running the following command:
```bash
sudo apt-get install bind9
```
8. Configure BIND to use your domain's nameservers by editing the `/etc/bind/named.conf.local` file. Add the following lines to the file:
```
zone "your_domain.com" {
    type master;
    file "/etc/bind/db.your_domain.com";
};

zone "your_domain.com" IN {
    NS ns1.your_domain.com.
    NS ns2.your_domain.com.
};

zone "ns1.your_domain.com" IN {
    type master;
    file "/etc/bind/db.ns1.your_domain.com";
};

zone "ns2.your_domain.com" IN {
    type master;
    file "/etc/bind/db.ns2.your_domain.com";
};
```
Replace `your_domain.com` with your actual domain name.
9. Create the named.conf.local file if it doesn't already exist. Run the following command:
```bash
sudo touch /etc/bind/db.your_domain.com
sudo touch /etc/bind/db.ns1.your_domain.com
sudo touch /etc/bind/db.ns2.your_domain.

