Here's an R code that checks if all non-NA elements in a character vector can be converted to numeric:

```R
# Function to check if all non-NA elements in a character vector can be converted to numeric
can_convert_to_numeric <- function(x) {
  x <- as.character(x) # Convert to character to handle NA values
  is.na(x) <- is.na(x) # Set NA values to TRUE

  # Check if all non-NA elements can be converted to numeric
  tryCatch({
    as.numeric(x[!is.na(x)])
  }, error = function(e) {
    return(FALSE)
  })
}

# Example usage
x <- c("1", "2", "3", "NA", "5")
print(can_convert_to_numeric(x)) # Output: TRUE

y <- c("1", "2", "3", "NA", "x")
print(can_convert_to_numeric(y)) # Output: FALSE
```

This function first converts the input character vector `x` to character to handle NA values. It then sets NA values to TRUE using the `is.na()` function. Finally, it uses a `tryCatch` block to attempt to convert the non-NA elements of `x` to numeric. If the conversion is successful, the function returns `TRUE`, otherwise it returns `FALSE`.

