@NestMiddleware()
export class MyMiddleware implements MiddlewareFunction {
  use(req, res, next) {
    // Your middleware logic here

    next();
  }
}

// Apply the EnvGuard decorator to the MyMiddleware class
MyMiddleware.use(new EnvGuard());
```

This way, the `EnvGuard` decorator will be applied to all instances of the `MyMiddleware` class, and it will only allow requests with `NODE_ENV` set to `true` to pass through.

Here's a simple decorator for your Nest.js middleware that checks the `NODE_ENV` variable and returns `false` if it's not set to `true`.

```typescript
import { Injectable, CanActivate, ExecutionContext } from '@nestjs/common';

@Injectable()
export class EnvGuard implements CanActivate {
  canActivate(context: ExecutionContext): boolean {
    const req = context.switchToHttp().getRequest();
