Here's a simple React utility to remove widows. This utility will check for any words that are broken across lines and join them together.

```javascript
import React, { useEffect, useState } from 'react';

const RemoveWidows = ({ text }) => {
  const [formattedText, setFormattedText] = useState('');

  useEffect(() => {
    const formatText = () => {
      const words = text.split(' ');
      const formattedWords = [];

      for (let i = 0; i < words.length; i++) {
        const word = words[i];
        const lastChar = word.charAt(word.length - 1);

        if (lastChar === ' ' || lastChar === '\n') {
          formattedWords.push(word);
        } else {
          const nextWord = words[i + 1];
          const nextLastChar = nextWord.charAt(0);

          if (nextLastChar === ' ' || nextLastChar === '\n') {
            formattedWords.push(word + ' ');
          } else {
            formattedWords.push(word);
          }
        }
      }

      setFormattedText(formattedWords.join(' '));
    };

    formatText();
  }, [text]);

  return <div>{formattedText}</div>;
};

export default RemoveWidows;
```

To use this utility, simply wrap your text with the `RemoveWidows` component:

```javascript
<RemoveWidows text="Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit." />
```

This will render the formatted text without any widows.

Here's a simple React utility to remove widows. This component will wrap your content and adjust the line breaks to prevent widows from occurring.

```javascript
import React, { useState } from 'react';

const WidowRemover = ({ children }) => {
  const [lines, setLines] = useState([]);

  const handleTextChange = (event) => {
    const text = event.target.value;
    const linesArray = text.split('\n');
    setLines(linesArray);
  };

  const renderLines = () => {
    return lines.map((line, index) => (
      <div key={index}>
        {line}
        <br />
      </div>
    ));
  };

  return (
    <div>
      <textarea value={lines.join('\n')} onChange={handleTextChange} />
      {renderLines()}
    </div>
  );
};

export default WidowRemover;
```

To use this component, simply wrap your content with it:

```javascript
